		Cybersecurity catalyst program, which is a 20-week intensive cybersecurity training in partnership with the
		<a href="https://www.sans.org/course/hacker-techniques-exploits-incident-handling" target="_blank">SANS Institute</a>,
		<a href="https://www.ryerson.ca/cybersecure-catalyst/" target="_blank">Ryerson University</a>, RBC, Rogers and the Government of Brampton to
		obtain two certifications from <a href="https://giac.org" target="_blank">GIAC</a>:
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li>GIAC Security Essentials Certification <a href="https://www.giac.org/certification/security-essentials-gsec" target="_blank">(GSEC)</a></li>
		<li>GIAC Certified Incident Handler <a href="https://www.giac.org/certification/certified-incident-handler-gcih" target="_blank">(GCIH)</a></li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		As an ITIL certified expert in service management, I have shown that with my strong belief in
		ethics, factored with being reliable, loyal, adaptable, hardworking, and motivated to perform above
